{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}{{ round_label }} · {{ site_name }}{% endblock %}
{% block description %}Pre-kickoff win/draw/loss probabilities for {{ round_label }}, fixed before the matches were played and never edited afterwards.{% endblock %}
{% block content %}

<h1 class="page-title">{{ round_label }}</h1>
<p class="lede">Match probabilities for Japan's J1 League. {{ payload.matches|length }} fixtures, fixed before kickoff.
<span class="callout--inline"><strong>The market is measurably better than this model</strong> &mdash; a disagreement below is a question, not an answer. <a href="methodology.html">Full caveat &amp; numbers</a>.</span></p>
<div class="table-scroll">
<table>
<caption>Calibrated model probabilities. Kickoff times are UTC, {{ payload.matches[0].commence_time[:4] }}. No market odds are shown here &mdash; see Methodology for why.</caption>
<thead>
<tr>
  <th scope="col">Kickoff</th>
  <th scope="col">Home</th>
  <th scope="col">Away</th>
  <th scope="col" class="num">P(H)</th>
  <th scope="col" class="num">P(D)</th>
  <th scope="col" class="num">P(A)</th>
  <th scope="col">Result</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
{% for m in payload.matches %}
{% set pmax = [m.p_calibrated.h, m.p_calibrated.d, m.p_calibrated.a]|max %}
<tr>
  <td>{{ m.commence_time|fmt_kickoff }}</td>
  <td>{{ m.home_team }}</td>
  <td>{{ m.away_team }}</td>
  <td class="num{% if m.p_calibrated.h == pmax %} num--max{% endif %}">{{ m.p_calibrated.h|fmt_pct }}</td>
  <td class="num{% if m.p_calibrated.d == pmax %} num--max{% endif %}">{{ m.p_calibrated.d|fmt_pct }}</td>
  <td class="num{% if m.p_calibrated.a == pmax %} num--max{% endif %}">{{ m.p_calibrated.a|fmt_pct }}</td>
  <td>
    {% if m.result %}
    {{ m.result.fthg|int }}&ndash;{{ m.result.ftag|int }} ({{ m.result.ftr }})
    {% if m.result.source == "odds_api_provisional" %}
    &middot; provisional
    {% endif %}
    {% if m.result.discrepancy %}
    <span class="badge badge--warn" title="odds-api provisional said {{ m.result.discrepancy.odds_api_provisional.fthg|int }}&ndash;{{ m.result.discrepancy.odds_api_provisional.ftag|int }} ({{ m.result.discrepancy.odds_api_provisional.ftr }}); football-data confirmed {{ m.result.discrepancy.football_data.fthg|int }}&ndash;{{ m.result.discrepancy.football_data.ftag|int }} ({{ m.result.discrepancy.football_data.ftr }})">discrepancy</span>
    {% endif %}
    {% else %}
    not yet played
    {% endif %}
  </td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>

{% if payload.round_summary %}
<h2>Round result</h2>
<p>
  {{ payload.round_summary.n_resolved }} of {{ payload.round_summary.n_matches }} fixtures resolved.
  {% if payload.round_summary.mean_rps_cal is not none %}
  Mean RPS (calibrated model): {{ '%.4f'|format(payload.round_summary.mean_rps_cal) }}.
  {% endif %}
  See <a href="record.html">Track Record</a> for the cumulative, non-backtest picture.
</p>
{% endif %}

<div class="callout">
  <p>Over {{ '{:,}'.format(run.n_matches) }} backtested J1 matches ({{ run.season_from }}&ndash;{{ run.season_to }}), the closing betting market scored {{ '%.4f'|format(run.d_rps) }} RPS points better than this model on average (95% CI [{{ '%.4f'|format(run.d_rps_ci_lo) }}, {{ '%.4f'|format(run.d_rps_ci_hi) }}]) &mdash; see <a href="methodology.html">Methodology</a>. This model has no information the market lacks: it does not see injuries, lineups, suspensions or travel. The bold figure in each row is only the most likely of three outcomes, not advice &mdash; in most football matches the most likely single outcome still loses more often than it wins.</p>
</div>

<details class="meta-details">
  <summary><h2>Metadata &amp; verification</h2></summary>

  <dl class="meta">
    <dt>Published (UTC)</dt><dd>{{ payload.generated_at|fmt_utc }}</dd>
    <dt>Trained as of (UTC)</dt><dd>{{ payload.asof|fmt_utc }}</dd>
    <dt>Model version</dt><dd>{{ payload.model_version }}</dd>
    <dt>params_hash</dt><dd>{{ payload.params_hash }}</dd>
    <dt>File SHA-256</dt><dd>{{ file_sha256 }}</dd>
    <dt>Market snapshot SHA-256</dt><dd>{{ payload.odds_snapshot.combined_sha256 }}</dd>
    <dt>Training window</dt><dd>{{ payload.training_window.n_matches }} matches, {{ payload.training_window.n_teams }} teams, since {{ payload.training_window.from_season }}</dd>
    <dt>Publish gate</dt>
    <dd>
      {% if payload.publish_gate.ok %}
      <span class="badge badge--ok">PASS</span>
      {% else %}
      <span class="badge badge--warn">BLOCKED</span>
      {% endif %}
    </dd>
  </dl>

  <h3>How to verify</h3>
  <p>
    This file is committed as <code>predictions/{{ source_filename }}</code> in the project's
    git repository, with the SHA-256 shown above. On its own, a git commit
    timestamp is <strong>not</strong> strong third-party evidence that a
    prediction existed before kickoff &mdash; the author can set it to any date.
    Independent timestamping (OpenTimestamps), Wayback Machine archiving and a
    GitHub Actions server-time witness are part of this project's published
    plan for closing that gap (design document, section&nbsp;3) and are not yet
    wired into this build. Until they are, verify what you can today: recompute
    the SHA-256 of the committed file yourself and confirm it matches the value
    above, and read the raw JSON &mdash; nothing on this page is derived from
    anything else.
  </p>
</details>

{% endblock %}
